  "title": "Financial depth",
  "href": "/topics/financial-depth",
  "dek": "How much saving and financing the domestic financial system can intermediate relative to the economy.",
  "intro": "Argentina combines substantial resident wealth with unusually shallow domestic credit and capital markets. That gap matters because a deeper local financial system can reduce dependence on volatile external financing, but rapid credit expansion also creates prudential risks if underwriting and borrower incomes do not keep pace.",
